---
import CopyCommand from "../../components/CopyCommand.astro";
import DocLayout from "../../layouts/DocLayout.astro";
---

<DocLayout
  title="Git signing"
  eyebrow="SECTION 06 / SIGNATURES"
  description="Use the same stable agent path for commit and tag signatures, whether the key is local or forwarded."
>
  <div class="prose">
    <h2>Configure Git for SSH signatures</h2>
    <CopyCommand command="git config --global gpg.format ssh" />
    <CopyCommand
      command="git config --global user.signingkey ~/.ssh/id_ed25519.pub"
    />
    <CopyCommand command="git config --global commit.gpgsign true" />
    <p>
      Git invokes <code>ssh-keygen</code>, which consults <code
        >SSH_AUTH_SOCK</code
      >. When that variable points at Lanyard, the requested public key can be
      signed by a forwarded laptop agent or by the local fallback.
    </p>
    <h2>Verify a commit</h2><CopyCommand
      command="git commit --allow-empty -m 'chore: verify signing'"
    /><CopyCommand command="git log --show-signature -1" />
    <h2>Allowed signers</h2><p>
      Verification is separate from signing. For local verification, configure
      Git’s <code>gpg.ssh.allowedSignersFile</code> with the identities you trust.
    </p>
    <pre><code>john@example.com ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAA...</code></pre>
    <div class="note">
      <strong>NO KEY COPYING</strong>The public key selects a signer. The
      private key stays inside its original agent throughout.
    </div>
  </div>
</DocLayout>
